          <p>
            Interior drains are usually priced per linear foot of wall, commonly in the range of $40 to $100, plus the pit and pump. A 140-foot perimeter at $70 a foot lands near $10,000 before extras such as wall membranes, additional pumps or concrete removal. Exterior work is priced by depth and access and can climb steeply when decks, stoops or driveways must be removed and replaced.
          </p>

          <p>
            Warranty terms are part of the price. Many contractors offer lifetime or transferable warranties on the drain, which can help resale, but read what they cover. A warranty that promises a dry basement is more valuable than one that only covers the pipe. Pumps typically carry separate, much shorter manufacturer warranties, often a few years.
          </p>
