          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most wet basements, the most dependable system is the simplest one that matches the leak: fixed gutters and grading, injected cracks, a coating on damp walls, and an interior perimeter drain with a cast-iron sump pump and battery backup only if water still enters along the floor. A combination unit like the Wayne WSS30V covers the pump side in one purchase.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Break every quote into parts, ask why each part is needed, and favor contractors who look outside before selling inside. Then maintain what you install: test both pumps, keep the discharge clear, and replace batteries and pumps on schedule.
